    "https://jobs.oakland.edu/postings/37992": {
      "title": "Special Instructor in Accounting",
      "description": "Oakland University Employment Site | Special Instructor in Accounting Skip to Main Content Employment Opportunities Toggle navigation Home Search Jobs Log In /Create Account Help Human Resources Benefits Campus Map Student Employment Special Instructor in Accounting Bookmark this Requisition Print Preview | Apply for this Job Please see Special Instructions for more details. Preference will be given to those that apply by July 11, 2026. Applications will be accepted until the position is filled. Posting Details Position Information Job Title Special Instructor in Accounting Department 0460 - Accounting & Finance Requisition No. 0000827 Job Description Summary The School of Business Administration at Oakland University seeks to fill a Special Instructor of Accounting position. This is a full-time position with job security track. The person who fills this position will likely teach graduate and/or undergraduate introductory financial and managerial accounting courses. Depending on her/his qualifications, the person may also teach data analytics in accounting, accounting information systems, taxation, and auditing. He/she will also work with the accounting student organizations and provide guidance on a career in accounting. The normal teaching load is seven classes per academic year. Class sizes are moderate. Summer teaching is usually available for an additional stipend. The successful candidate will provide evidence of effective teaching or training, relevant professional experience, and experience interacting with business professionals. Candidates must demonstrate effective communication skills. The ability to collaborate effectively with other faculty members, intent to engage in scholarly/professional activity, and evidence of professional accomplishments are desirable. The salary is competitive, and the fringe benefits are excellent. Minimum Qualifications Masters in Accounting, JD, ( LLM is a plus), or equivalent Professional license (e.g. CPA ) Special Instructions to Applicants Preference will be given to those that apply by July 11, 2026. Applications will be accepted until the position is filled. School/College & Department/Program Summary More About Oakland University The University is located on 1,443 acres of scenic land in the cities of Rochester Hills and Auburn Hills in Oakland County, Michigan. The University offers 142 bachelor’s degree programs and 138 graduate degree and certificate programs. Academics include programs in the College of Arts and Sciences, School of Business Administration, School of Education and Human Services, School of Engineering and Computer Science, School of Health Sciences, School of Medicine and School of Nursing. As an anchor institution in southeastern Michigan that is dedicated to building ongoing, collaborative relationships, Oakland University embraces community and civic engagement to enhance the lives of its students and positively impact the broader community. Learn more about Oakland University’s Mission & Vision and Strategic Plan . Pay Basis Open Date 06/04/2026 Open Until Filled Yes Job Category Full-time Faculty EEO Statement Oakland University is an Equal Opportunity institution. Posting Specific Questions Required fields are indicated with an asterisk (*). Applicant Documents Required Documents Curriculum Vitae (CV) Cover Letter Transcripts (unofficial) Teaching Statement Optional Documents Teaching Evaluation Teaching Philosophy 371 Wilson Boulevard, Rochester, MI 48309 248-370-2100     To ensure the security of your data, you will be logged out due to inactivity in 3 minutes at . Any data not saved will be lost. Click 'OK' to keep your session active."
