    "https://jobs.oakland.edu/postings/33693": {
      "title": "Position Information",
      "description": "Oakland University Employment Site | Pontiac Community Interviewer Skip to Main Content Employment Opportunities Toggle navigation Home Search Jobs Log In /Create Account Help Human Resources Benefits Campus Map Student Employment Pontiac Community Interviewer Bookmark this Requisition Print Preview | Apply for this Job Posting Details Posting Details Position Title Pontiac Community Interviewer Department 2055 - Human Development & Child Study Position Number E39854 Requisition No. TC05575 Salary Range/Pay Rate $25 per hour Benefits of Working at Oakland University No benefits are associated with this casual position. Employee Group/Grade Casual Job Category Casual Posted Casual/Temp Classification Work Schedule Casual (19hrs or less, No Benefits ) Shift/Days Pay Schedule Hour Number of Hrs./Wk. 4 Position Information Position Information Employee's Effective Start Date 10/17/2024 If this is a Temporary position, provide end date or enter N/A for any other position type. 08/30/2026 Minimum Qualifications Extensive lived experience in Pontiac Have interest in education and/or care of young children, birth through age 3 Responsible, dependable, and able to think on their feet and problem solve Excellent interpersonal, oral and written communication skills Comfortable using a digital recorder or additional technology, such as Zoom, or ability to learn quickly Amplia experiencia de vida en Pontiac Tener interés en la educación y / o el cuidado de los niños pequeños, desde el nacimiento hasta los 3 años de edad Responsable, confiable, y capaz de pensar en sus pies y resolver problemas Excelentes habilidades de comunicación interpersonal, oral y escrita Cómodo usando una grabadora digital o tecnología adicional, como Zoom, o capacidad para aprender rápidamente Desired Qualifications Strong interest in early childhood education Proficiency in Spanish, Hmong, or Arabic. Gran interés por la educación infantil Dominio del español, hmong o árabe Position Purpose The Oakland University-Pontiac Initiative, Early Childhood Education ( OUPIECE ) group and the Department of Human Development and Child Studies ( HDCS ) at Oakland University, in partnership with Pontiac School District ( PSD ) invite applications to the Pontiac Community Interviewer position to work on a newly funded project to co-design an infant-toddler center and resource hub at Pontiac High School (Baby PEACE ). El grupo de la Iniciativa Oakland University-Pontiac, Educación Infantil Temprana ( OUPIECE ) y el Departamento de Desarrollo Humano y Estudios Infantiles ( HDCS ) de la Universidad de Oakland, en asociación con el Distrito Escolar de Pontiac ( PSD ) invitan solicitantes para el puesto de Entrevistador de la Comunidad de Pontiac para trabajar en un proyecto recientemente financiado para co-diseñar un centro para bebés y niños pequeños y un centro de recursos en Pontiac High School (Baby PEACE ). Job Duties As a Pontiac Community Interviewer, you will be a part of the community-led research team. We seek an individual who has extensive knowledge of the Pontiac community and is adept in collecting community feedback through interviews or focus groups (using a co-developed protocol) about the design of Baby PEACE . No prior research experience is needed. However, applicants must pass the CITI (human subjects research ethics) training prior to full hire. In addition, training on how to do focus groups and interviews will be provided. $25/hour for up to 100 hours across two years. Position begins immediately and ends on August 30, 2026. Como entrevistador de la comunidad de Pontiac, formará parte del equipo de investigación dirigido por la comunidad. Buscamos a una persona que tenga un amplio conocimiento de la comunidad de Pontiac y sea experta en la recopilación de opiniones de la comunidad a través de entrevistas o grupos focales (utilizando un protocolo co-desarrollado) sobre el diseño de Baby PEACE . No se requiere experiencia previa en investigación. Sin embargo, los solicitantes deben aprobar la formación CITI (ética de la investigación con sujetos humanos) antes de la contratación completa. Además, se proporcionará formación sobre cómo realizar grupos focales y entrevistas. 25 $/hora por un máximo de 100 horas a lo largo de dos años. El puesto comienza inmediatamente y finaliza el 30 de agosto de 2026. Job Open Date 10/03/2024 Job Close Date Open Until Filled Yes Position Specific Questions Required fields are indicated with an asterisk (*). Documents Needed to Apply Required Documents Cover Letter List of References Resume Optional Documents 371 Wilson Boulevard, Rochester, MI 48309 248-370-2100     To ensure the security of your data, you will be logged out due to inactivity in 3 minutes at . Any data not saved will be lost. Click 'OK' to keep your session active."
    },
