    "https://jobs.oakland.edu/postings/38943": {
      "title": "Position Information",
      "description": "Oakland University Employment Site | Core Infrastructure Engineer Skip to Main Content Employment Opportunities Toggle navigation Home Search Jobs Log In /Create Account Help Human Resources Benefits Campus Map Student Employment Core Infrastructure Engineer Bookmark this Requisition Print Preview | Apply for this Job Posting Details Posting Details Position Title Core Infrastructure Engineer Department 2167 - University Technology Services Position Number 986475 Requisition No. S02688 Salary Range/Pay Rate $76,875 annually. Benefits of Working at Oakland University Oakland University offers competitive salaries and an excellent benefit program including a comprehensive medical plan with low contribution amounts for our employees, dental and vision plans at no cost for our employees, generous paid time off plans, a generous University contribution to our 403(b) retirement plan, tuition assistance for our employees and dependents, free access to our Campus Recreation Center and workout facilities, and flexible work schedules and wellness programs. These are current benefit levels subject to future changes. Employee Group/Grade AP Band R Job Category Administrative-Professional Work Schedule FT/Reg (40 hours) Shift/Days This is a full-time position. First consideration will be given to those who apply by March 10, 2026. Pay Schedule Month Number of Hrs./Wk. 40 Position Information Position Information Minimum Qualifications Bachelor’s degree in Computer Science, Information Systems, or a related field, or an equivalent combination of education and experience. A minimum of four (4) years of experience in systems administration, collaboration platforms, or infrastructure engineering. Advanced administration and troubleshooting experience with Google Workspace (Gmail, Calendar, Drive, Groups), including configuration, security, and performance optimization. Working knowledge of cloud platforms and services, including Microsoft Azure, Amazon Web Services ( AWS ), Google Cloud Platform ( GCP ), and Microsoft 365. Experience supporting enterprise email systems, including routing, security, and troubleshooting. Experience with identity and access management tools (Microsoft Entra ID, MFA , SSO , conditional access). Scripting and automation experience. Knowledge of patch management, system updates, and monitoring of core infrastructure services. Understanding of networking fundamentals, DNS , certificates, and cloud security best practices. Strong troubleshooting, analytical, and problem-solving skills. Strong communication and customer service skills. Ability to manage multiple priorities and work both independently and collaboratively. Willingness to work scheduled maintenance windows, including occasional overnight hours. Must reside in the state of Michigan and be able to report to campus within 1–1.5 hours if required. Ability to travel occasionally for professional development or training. Desired Qualifications Master’s degree in Computer Science, Information Systems, or a related field. Experience supporting IT services in higher education or other public sector organizations. Experience managing large-scale or multi-domain enterprise environments. Experience with governance, compliance, or data protection frameworks in regulated environments. Experience leading technical projects or cross-functional initiatives. Experience with virtualization and container solutions (e.g., VMware, Kubernetes, Docker). Industry certifications relevant to enterprise systems, identity management, or collaboration platforms. All Qualifications Unless otherwise required by an applicable collective bargaining agreement, all minimum, additional and desired qualifications are preferred, but qualifications, degrees, and/or experience deemed comparable and/or equivalent by Oakland University in its sole and exclusive discretion may be considered. Position Details Position Purpose University Technology Services, the central IT organization of Oakland University, is seeking a Core Services Engineer to perform technology tasks. The Core Services Engineer is responsible for the administration, maintenance, and optimization of the organization’s core infrastructure and collaboration platforms—with a primary focus on Google Workspace and supporting responsibilities for Microsoft 365 and cloud identity services – Microsoft Entra ID. This position ensures secure, reliable, and efficient delivery of essential IT services while driving automation, standardization, and continuous improvement. The Core Services Engineer collaborates across IT teams to enhance productivity, streamline operations, and ensure seamless integration between Google and Microsoft ecosystems. The role requires a deep understanding of email services, including troubleshooting, configuration, and optimization to support institutional communication needs. Key Responsibilities Serve as the primary administrator and subject matter expert for Google Workspace, including Gmail, Drive, Shared Drives, Groups, and collaboration services, ensuring secure, reliable, and high-performing operations. Administer and maintain enterprise email services, including configuration, routing, security controls, troubleshooting, and performance optimization. Support and maintain core services operating within cloud and hosted environments, ensuring reliability, security, and alignment with institutional standards. Ensure the reliability, security, and performance of core collaboration and infrastructure services. Perform routine system maintenance, including patching, updates, upgrades, and service monitoring to maintain system integrity and compliance. Develop and maintain automation scripts, configuration standards, and operational documentation to improve efficiency and service consistency. Lead or support system migrations, platform integrations, and service improvement initiatives related to collaboration and enterprise systems. Participate in enterprise patch management and coordinate maintenance communications to minimize service disruption. Collaborate with IT leadership and cross-functional teams to align core services with institutional needs and service standards. The best things about this position are: The teamwork; you are a member of a talented team. The ability to learn and grow professionally. We provide many opportunities to continue to advance your knowledge and professional skills. Your work matters to the students, faculty, and employees at the University. The University offers an attractive benefits package that includes excellent healthcare and tuition benefits for employees and their families, flexible work schedules, paid vacation, wellness programs, friendly campus events, and generous retirement contributions. Job Open Date 02/25/2026 Job Close Date Position Specific Questions Required fields are indicated with an asterisk (*). * Are you currently a member of the Oakland University Administrative-Professional Group? Yes No No Response * In less than 10 sentences, please describe your experience architecting, planing, designing and implementing information technology solutions? (Open Ended Question) Documents Needed to Apply Required Documents Cover Letter Resume Writing Sample Optional Documents 371 Wilson Boulevard, Rochester, MI 48309 248-370-2100     To ensure the security of your data, you will be logged out due to inactivity in 3 minutes at . Any data not saved will be lost. Click 'OK' to keep your session active."
    },
    "https://jobs.oakland.edu/postings/38065": {
      "title": "Position Information",
      "description": "Oakland University Employment Site | Athletics Facility Event Staff Skip to Main Content Employment Opportunities Toggle navigation Home Search Jobs Log In /Create Account Help Human Resources Benefits Campus Map Student Employment Athletics Facility Event Staff Bookmark this Requisition Print Preview | Apply for this Job Posting Details Posting Details Position Title Athletics Facility Event Staff Department 2836 - Athletics Administration Position Number E44266 Requisition No. TC06433 Salary Range/Pay Rate 15.00 hr. Benefits of Working at Oakland University No benefits are associated with this position. Employee Group/Grade Casual Job Category Casual /Temporary Casual/Temp Classification Work Schedule Casual (19hrs or less, No Benefits ) Shift/Days Pay Schedule Hour Number of Hrs./Wk. 19 Position Information Position Information Employee's Effective Start Date 06/15/2026 If this is a Temporary position, provide end date or enter N/A for any other position type. n/a Minimum Qualifications High school diploma or equivalent. Ability to work evenings, weekends, holidays, and flexible schedules based on event needs. Ability to stand, walk, and remain active for extended periods. Ability to lift and move up to 30 pounds. Strong interpersonal and customer service skills. Ability to work effectively as part of a team. Reliable transportation and dependable attendance. Desired Qualifications Previous experience in event operations, facility management, customer service, hospitality, recreation, or athletics. Experience working athletic contests, tournaments, concerts, or special events. Familiarity with NCAA Division I athletics. Current Oakland University student or recent graduate preferred. Experience working with diverse populations and providing exceptional customer service. Basic knowledge of event safety and crowd management practices. Position Purpose The Facility Event Staff position supports the successful operation of Oakland University Athletics facilities and game-day events. This casual role assists with event setup and breakdown, guest services, facility preparation, crowd management, and operational support to ensure a safe, welcoming, and professional environment for student-athletes, coaches, officials, fans, and guests. Facility Event Staff serve as representatives of Oakland University Athletics and play an important role in delivering a first-class event experience. Job Duties Event Setup & Breakdown Assist with the setup and breakdown of athletic contests, practices, camps, and special events. Arrange tables, chairs, signage, barricades, hospitality areas, and other event equipment. Prepare competition venues and support spaces according to event requirements. Assist with post-event cleanup and facility reset. Facility Operations Monitor assigned facility areas during events. Conduct routine inspections of event spaces and report maintenance or safety concerns. Assist in maintaining a clean, organized, and professional environment. Ensure designated areas remain accessible and event-ready. Guest Services Provide directions and assistance to fans, participants, officials, and visitors. Answer general questions regarding facilities and event operations. Provide excellent customer service while maintaining a positive and professional demeanor. Event Support Assist game management personnel with operational needs during athletic events. Assist with crowd management and emergency response procedures under staff direction. Support special events, tournaments, camps, and community engagement activities. Safety & Compliance Follow University, departmental, and facility policies and procedures. Report accidents, incidents, safety hazards, or facility concerns immediately. Assist in maintaining a safe environment for all event participants and guests. Other Duties This position requires work in indoor and outdoor athletic facilities under varying weather conditions. Duties involve standing, walking, lifting, carrying equipment, and performing physical event support tasks for extended periods. Work schedules are based on athletic competition and event calendars and include evenings, weekends, and occasional holidays. Perform other related duties as assigned to support Athletics event and facility operations. Job Open Date Job Close Date Open Until Filled No Position Specific Questions Required fields are indicated with an asterisk (*). Documents Needed to Apply Required Documents Cover Letter Resume Optional Documents 371 Wilson Boulevard, Rochester, MI 48309 248-370-2100     To ensure the security of your data, you will be logged out due to inactivity in 3 minutes at . Any data not saved will be lost. Click 'OK' to keep your session active."
    },
    "https://jobs.oakland.edu/postings/38980": {
      "title": "Laboratory Stockroom Coordinator",
      "description": "Oakland University Employment Site | Laboratory Stockroom Coordinator Skip to Main Content Employment Opportunities Toggle navigation Home Search Jobs Log In /Create Account Help Human Resources Benefits Campus Map Student Employment Laboratory Stockroom Coordinator Bookmark this Requisition Print Preview | Apply for this Job Posting Details Posting Details Position Title Laboratory Stockroom Coordinator Department 0305 - Biological Sciences Position Number 986403 Requisition No. S02808 Salary Range/Pay Rate $54,272 annually Benefits of Working at Oakland University This position is an Oakland University Professional Support Association- MEA / NEA position. The incumbent will be represented by the MEA / NEA . This position will remain open a minimum of five (5) working days. External applicants may be considered. Qualified bargaining unit members will receive interviews. Employee Group/Grade C-9 Job Category Clerical-Technical Work Schedule FT/Reg (40 hours) Shift/Days This is a full-time position working on campus with limited remote, occasional nights and weekends may be necessary. Occasional work location at LORACS and BioPreserve. Pay Schedule Month Number of Hrs./Wk. 40hr/wk Position Information Position Information Minimum Qualifications Bachelor’s degree and/or equivalent training and some experience in a specific discipline such that mastery of standard methods, procedures, terminology and techniques can be demonstrated and adapted to the laboratory setting. Knowledge of “scientific equipment” used in teaching and routine preparation. Ability to establish and maintain up-to-date inventory records. Ability to effectively interact with the public, students, faculty and staff. Must be comfortable working outdoors in varying weather conditions and may be exposed to dirt and/or mud. Must be proficient in Microsoft Office Suite and Google Suite. Desired Qualifications Bachelor of Science or equivalent combination of education and experience in Biological Science or Chemistry with knowledge of laboratory safety, biosafety and hazardous waste protocols. All Qualifications Unless otherwise required by an applicable collective bargaining agreement, all minimum, additional and desired qualifications are preferred, but qualifications, degrees, and/or experience deemed comparable and/or equivalent by Oakland University in its sole and exclusive discretion may be considered. Position Details Must be well organized, able to prioritize, self-motivated, and work collaboratively with faculty, students, and community partners. Position Purpose To be responsible for all of the departmental instructional laboratories. Coordinate laboratory activities including preparing solutions, setting up weekly experiments for all laboratory courses, ordering stockroom supplies, and ensuring that the equipment and facilities are in proper working condition. Job Open Date 08/07/2026 Job Close Date Position Specific Questions Required fields are indicated with an asterisk (*). * Are you a member of the Oakland University Professional Support Association-MEA/NEA? Yes No No Response * Describe your experience with instructional  laboratory courses. (Open Ended Question) Documents Needed to Apply Required Documents Cover Letter Resume Optional Documents 371 Wilson Boulevard, Rochester, MI 48309 248-370-2100     To ensure the security of your data, you will be logged out due to inactivity in 3 minutes at . Any data not saved will be lost. Click 'OK' to keep your session active."
