    "https://jobs.oakland.edu/postings/38982": {
      "title": "Office Assistant III",
      "description": "Oakland University Employment Site | Office Assistant III Skip to Main Content Employment Opportunities Toggle navigation Home Search Jobs Log In /Create Account Help Human Resources Benefits Campus Map Student Employment Office Assistant III Bookmark this Requisition Print Preview | Apply for this Job Posting Details Posting Details Position Title Office Assistant III Department 1495 - Sociology, Anthropology, Social Work and Criminal Justice Position Number 993438 Requisition No. S02823 Salary Range/Pay Rate $51,067 annually Benefits of Working at Oakland University This position is an Oakland University Professional Support Association- MEA / NEA position. The incumbent will be represented by the MEA / NEA . This position will remain open a minimum of five (5) working days. External applicants may be considered. Qualified bargaining unit members will receive interviews. Employee Group/Grade C-8 Job Category Clerical-Technical Work Schedule FT/Reg (40 hours) Shift/Days This is a full-time position. Remote work possible after adequate training period. Pay Schedule Month Number of Hrs./Wk. 40hr/wk Position Information Position Information Minimum Qualifications High school graduation or an equivalent combination of education and experience. Four years progressively responsible office experience, including direct experience in office coordination, i.e., prioritizing work assignments, maintaining work flow to meet deadlines. Ability to compose correspondence. Ability to operate standard office equipment. Ability to effectively interact with the public, students, faculty and staff. Knowledge of proper grammar, spelling and punctuation and ability to utilize proper standard office source manuals. Possess the keyboarding skills necessary to perform successfully in this position. Experience in clerical accounting/bookkeeping. Ability to work under pressure. Ability to perform the functions consistent with intermediate word processing and intermediate spreadsheet applications as demonstrated by a skills assessment. Desired Qualifications All Qualifications Unless otherwise required by an applicable collective bargaining agreement, all minimum, additional and desired qualifications are preferred, but qualifications, degrees, and/or experience deemed comparable and/or equivalent by Oakland University in its sole and exclusive discretion may be considered. Position Details Provide support for the Department of Sociology, Anthropology, Social Work & Criminal Justice including specialized office assistance, coordinating procedural business or service activities for a complex academic area involving processing, implementing, advising and/or reporting specialized subject matter. Duties include course scheduling, curriculum input, financial/general bookkeeping duties. Position Purpose To provide specialized office assistance, coordinating procedural business or service activities for a complex program area involving processing, implementing, advising on, and reporting specialized subject matter. Job Open Date 08/27/2026 Job Close Date Position Specific Questions Required fields are indicated with an asterisk (*). * Are you a member of the Oakland University Professional Support Association-MEA/NEA? Yes No No Response Describe your current experience with bookkeeping/clerical accounting, including payroll, payment vouchers, purchasing and reconciling accounts. (Open Ended Question) Describe your experience in course scheduling, include any software you have used to assist in scheduling. (Open Ended Question) Documents Needed to Apply Required Documents Cover Letter Resume Optional Documents 371 Wilson Boulevard, Rochester, MI 48309 248-370-2100     To ensure the security of your data, you will be logged out due to inactivity in 3 minutes at . Any data not saved will be lost. Click 'OK' to keep your session active."
