    "https://jobs.oakland.edu/postings/34439": {
      "title": "Assistant Professor of Physical Therapy",
      "description": "Oakland University Employment Site | Assistant Professor of Physical Therapy Skip to Main Content Employment Opportunities Toggle navigation Home Search Jobs Log In /Create Account Help Human Resources Benefits Campus Map Student Employment Assistant Professor of Physical Therapy Bookmark this Requisition Print Preview | Apply for this Job Posting Details Position Information Job Title Assistant Professor of Physical Therapy Department 0738 - Human Movement Science Requisition No. 0000770 Job Description Summary The Physical Therapy Program in the Department of Human Movement Science at Oakland University (Rochester, MI) invites applications for a tenure-track Assistant Professor position starting August 15, 2025. This is a unique growth opportunity to join a supportive faculty with excellent resources, balancing teaching, research, and service. Teaching: Contribute expertise across our Physical Therapy programs, including the Doctor of Physical Therapy ( DPT ), graduate/post-professional certificates (Orthopedic Manual PT, Oncology Rehab, Teaching & Learning), and Ph.D. in Human Movement Science. Research: Receive support and mentorship to establish a peer-reviewed research agenda, leveraging state-of-the-art labs, clinical partnerships, and strengths in upstream care and community engagement. Service: Strengthen relationships with clinical partners, contribute to student recruitment and retention, and enhance academic programs and professional organizations. Oakland University values an inclusive commitment to teaching, research, and service. We encourage applications from individuals who can broaden and advance our strengths in foundational and clinical sciences. Those with board certifications orgraduate certificates are especially encouraged to apply. Minimum Qualifications 1. Hold/obtain a Michigan Physical Therapy License 2. A CAPTE -recognized terminal academic degree (PhD, EdD, DSc, DHS , or equivalent) or ABD if applicant holds a DPT degree 3. Three years of clinical experience in physical therapy 4. Teaching experience in an academic physical therapy program 6. Record of scholarly activities 7. Demonstrate compatibility with current faculty 8. Support for goals, mission, vision and philosophy of the program 9. Perceived fit within the needs of the program Special Instructions to Applicants School/College & Department/Program Summary The School of Health Sciences serves about 1750 undergraduate, masters, doctoral, and post-professional students through a singular model of advancing community-engaged translational relationships and connecting theory to best practices. Building upon the foundations of the natural and behavioral sciences we are organized departmentally into four themes: Public and Environmental Wellness, Interdisciplinary Health Sciences, Clinical and Diagnostic Sciences, and Human Movement Science. The Department of Human Movement Science ( HMS ) offers the bachelor (BS), clinical professional ( DPT ), and post-professional degrees and certificates. Our programs span exercise science ( EXS ), physical therapy (PT), and uniquely, orthotics and prosthetics (O&P).We operate multiple teaching/research labs available to faculty members, for PT (Acute Care Simulation, Musculoskeletal, Neurorehabilitation); for EXS (Exercise Physiology, Biomechanics Ergonomics Abilities Research, Strength and Fitness); and for O&P (Orthotics and Prosthetics Fabrication). Oakland University offers distinct research support and mentoring through a number of opportunities including: by the University, an active scholarly community, competitively available faculty grants, grant writing workshops and support through the Research Office; and distinctlyby the School of Health Sciences, Seed and Sprout Grants and the PT FacultyResearch Grants, supervision and mentoring of graduate students, including research doctoral students (where qualified). Our Physical Therapy Program provides strong connections to theclinical community, features service engagement through pro bono and health andwellness programs, and our faculty are nationally and internationally recognized for theirresearch and clinical expertise. Our beautiful platinum LEED -certified campus facilities and broad clinical andcommunity-based opportunities offer an ideal supportive environment for students,faculty, staff and partners to create and enjoy innovative learning, meaningful service,and vibrant research pursuits – in purpose for health. More About Oakland University The University is located on 1,443 acres of scenic land in the cities of Rochester Hills and Auburn Hills in Oakland County, Michigan. The University offers 142 bachelor’s degree programs and 138 graduate degree and certificate programs. Academics include programs in the College of Arts and Sciences, School of Business Administration, School of Education and Human Services, School of Engineering and Computer Science, School of Health Sciences, School of Medicine and School of Nursing. As an anchor institution in southeastern Michigan that is dedicated to building ongoing, collaborative relationships, Oakland University embraces community and civic engagement to enhance the lives of its students and positively impact the broader community. Learn more about Oakland University’s Mission & Vision and Strategic Plan . Pay Basis Open Date 04/02/2025 Open Until Filled Yes Job Category Full-time Faculty EEO Statement Oakland University is an Affirmative Action/Equal Opportunity Employer and encourages applications from women and minorities. Posting Specific Questions Required fields are indicated with an asterisk (*). Applicant Documents Required Documents Curriculum Vitae (CV) Cover Letter Transcripts (unofficial) Teaching Statement List of References Proof of Physical Therapy License Optional Documents 371 Wilson Boulevard, Rochester, MI 48309 248-370-2100     To ensure the security of your data, you will be logged out due to inactivity in 3 minutes at . Any data not saved will be lost. Click 'OK' to keep your session active."
    },
    "https://jobs.oakland.edu/postings/38726": {
      "title": "GSRP Evaluation Data Collector Position: Clare-Gladwin Counties",
      "description": "Oakland University Employment Site | GSRP Evaluation Data Collector Position: Clare-Gladwin Counties Skip to Main Content Employment Opportunities Toggle navigation Home Search Jobs Log In /Create Account Help Human Resources Benefits Campus Map Student Employment GSRP Evaluation Data Collector Position: Clare-Gladwin Counties Bookmark this Requisition Print Preview | Apply for this Job Posting Details Posting Details Position Title GSRP Evaluation Data Collector Position: Clare-Gladwin Counties Department 2055 - Human Development & Child Study Position Number E36678 Requisition No. TC06465 Salary Range/Pay Rate $26 per hour Benefits of Working at Oakland University No benefits are associated with this position. Employee Group/Grade Casual Job Category Casual Posted Casual/Temp Classification Work Schedule Casual (19hrs or less, No Benefits ) Shift/Days We are seeking applicants available for 2–3 weekday mornings during preschool classroom hours in September–October and April–May to conduct in-person child assessments. Some afternoon and/or evening availability will also be needed to complete required post-assessment paperwork. Pay Schedule Hour Number of Hrs./Wk. 5-7 Position Information Position Information Employee's Effective Start Date 08/24/2026 If this is a Temporary position, provide end date or enter N/A for any other position type. 08/30/2027 Minimum Qualifications Experience working with preschool children Available to work week-day morning hours Must have reliable transportation Ability to follow specific, standardized protocols Strong organizational skills Excellent interpersonal, oral and written communication skills Willingness to learn new technology Desired Qualifications Familiarity with Michigan’s state-funded Prekindergarten program, Great Start Readiness Program ( GSRP ), and Michigan’s early childhood landscape Prior experience conducting child assessments in early childhood classrooms Position Purpose The Department of Human Development and Child Studies ( HDCS ), housed in the School of Education and Human Services, invites applications for several part-time Data Collector positions to work on a statewide preschool evaluation. We are seeking applicants available for 2–3 weekday mornings during preschool classroom hours in September–October and April–May to conduct in-person child assessments. Some afternoon and/or evening availability will also be needed to complete required post-assessment paperwork. Job Duties Responsibilities include completing a mandatory training to be held in late August (date TBD ), contacting teachers to arrange – mutually-agreed upon times to assess study children in their classrooms, driving to sites in the counties of Clare and Gladwin, and additional tasks as assigned. Must pass a background check prior to hiring/starting. Job Open Date 08/14/2026 Job Close Date Open Until Filled No Position Specific Questions Required fields are indicated with an asterisk (*). Documents Needed to Apply Required Documents Cover Letter List of References Resume Optional Documents 371 Wilson Boulevard, Rochester, MI 48309 248-370-2100     To ensure the security of your data, you will be logged out due to inactivity in 3 minutes at . Any data not saved will be lost. Click 'OK' to keep your session active."
