    "https://jobs.oakland.edu/postings/38808": {
      "title": "Development Associate",
      "description": "Oakland University Employment Site | Development Associate - School of Health Sciences Skip to Main Content Employment Opportunities Toggle navigation Home Search Jobs Log In /Create Account Help Human Resources Benefits Campus Map Student Employment Development Associate - School of Health Sciences Bookmark this Requisition Print Preview | Apply for this Job Posting Details Posting Details Position Title Development Associate - School of Health Sciences Department 0070 - Health Sciences Position Number E30155 Requisition No. TC06497 Salary Range/Pay Rate $25 per hour Benefits of Working at Oakland University There are no benefits with this position. Employee Group/Grade Casual Job Category Casual Posted Casual/Temp Classification Work Schedule Casual (19hrs or less, No Benefits ) Shift/Days TBD . Note: Evening and weekend hours may occasionally be required. Pay Schedule Hour Number of Hrs./Wk. Up to 19 hours per week Position Information Position Information Employee's Effective Start Date 09/01/2026 If this is a Temporary position, provide end date or enter N/A for any other position type. N/A Minimum Qualifications Bachelor’s Degree or an equivalent combination of education and/or experience. One to two years’ experience in development, fundraising, program management or an equivalent combination. Excellent oral and written communication skills along with keen attention to detail. Experience writing and editing executive level communications and advancement content. Knowledge of technology and its application to development and fundraising activities. Previous experience with database and records management. Excellent organizational and analytical skills. Ability to communicate effectively with donors and university staff at all levels. Discretion and sound judgment in dealing with confidential information. Self-starter with creative ability to work efficiently and accurately to meet critical deadlines. Desired Qualifications Previous experience in university environment or non-profit is preferred. Position Purpose The Development Associate (DA) will support and facilitate development office projects, excluding major gift work, for the School of Health Sciences. They will take responsibility for development functions including donor stewardship outreach and communications; annual fund efforts; supporting fundraising and donor engagement events; gift processing; and other development related efforts not directly linked to cultivating and soliciting major gifts. The DA is also responsible for writing and preparing executive level communication, custom acknowledgement letters, donor impact reports, and providing proposal writing support. The DA will report to the Director of Philanthropy, School of Nursing & School of Health Sciences and must have experience in managing multiple tasks and a good working knowledge ofdevelopment. Note: Evening and weekend hours may occasionally be required. Job Duties Lead efforts for drafting and preparing executive level communications, donor acknowledgment letters, donor impact reports, and other donor cultivation & stewardship materials produced by SHS . This includes story gathering and securing thank you notes from student scholarship recipients. Will support proposal development efforts led by the Director of Philanthropy. Works closely with Director of Philanthropy, annual giving team and unit faculty and staff to conduct annual giving campaigns such as Giving Day, OUFD , unit specific appeals, etc. Assist with Advisory Board engagement activities. Provide support for SHS fundraising events, with an emphasis on sponsor fulfillment. Support other donor cultivation and stewardship events as needed. Assist with improvement of SHS development office processes, as well as processes of others impacted by SHS donor engagement. To include management of SHS fundraising files. Provide administrative support for Director of Philanthropy as needed. Job Open Date 08/21/2026 Job Close Date Open Until Filled Yes Position Specific Questions Required fields are indicated with an asterisk (*). Documents Needed to Apply Required Documents Cover Letter Resume Optional Documents 371 Wilson Boulevard, Rochester, MI 48309 248-370-2100     To ensure the security of your data, you will be logged out due to inactivity in 3 minutes at . Any data not saved will be lost. Click 'OK' to keep your session active."
