    "https://jobs.oakland.edu/postings/38281": {
      "title": "Position Information",
      "description": "Oakland University Employment Site | Temp IT Financial/Budget Analyst Skip to Main Content Employment Opportunities Toggle navigation Home Search Jobs Log In /Create Account Help Human Resources Benefits Campus Map Student Employment Temp IT Financial/Budget Analyst Bookmark this Requisition Print Preview | Apply for this Job Posting Details Posting Details Position Title Temp IT Financial/Budget Analyst Department 2167 - University Technology Services Position Number X12643 Requisition No. TC06448 Salary Range/Pay Rate 25.00 Benefits of Working at Oakland University There are no benefits with this position. Employee Group/Grade Temporary Job Category Temporary Posted Casual/Temp Classification Work Schedule FT/Temp (40 hours, No Benefits) Shift/Days Pay Schedule Hour Number of Hrs./Wk. 40 Position Information Position Information Employee's Effective Start Date 07/01/2026 If this is a Temporary position, provide end date or enter N/A for any other position type. 12/31/2026 Minimum Qualifications Bachelor’s degree in finance, accounting, business administration, or a related field, or an equivalent combination of education and/or experience. A minimum of two (2) years of experience in a financial skillset related to accounting, budgeting, cost analysis, forecasting, financial reporting, and/or similar experience. Strong proficiency in spreadsheets, using but not limited to (MS Excel, Google Sheets, etc.) Proficiency with data analysis tools, including Excel, and/or budgeting software. Excellent Microsoft and Google Workspace skills. Experience in clerical accounting/bookkeeping. Ability to analyze and track contracts along with software and support renewals. Effective oral and written communication skills. Strong analytical and organizational skills. Ability to effectively collaborate with university constituents. Ability to work well with all levels of employees and understand the need for confidentiality. Ability to work under pressure. Ability to multitask. Desired Qualifications Master’s degree. Course work or certifications in Accounting. Proficiency with data analysis tools SQL , and/or advanced budgeting software. Experience in Higher Education and their accounting principles. Experience with Enterprise Resource Planning or ERP (Banner) or others. Experience in GAAP \\ Fund Based Accounting. Experience working in IT or relevant education a plus. Any experience in IT contract management and compliance. Position Purpose Job Duties The information technology (IT) Financial/Budget Analyst, reporting through the IT Business Operations department, serves as a key resource for financial planning for University Technology Services ( UTS ) at Oakland University and coordinates among technical units to help ensure efficient, strategic financial resource planning. Main responsibilities include: ● Coordinating directly with the CIO and IT leadership staff to develop the UTS budget ● Tracking and monitoring UTS expenditures and working to ensure purchases align with budgetary constraints and cost-saving initiatives ● Developing plans for the appropriate allocation of resources to IT departments ● Overseeing critical tasks such as cost management, funding proposals, grants management, and financial reporting ● Regularly collaborating with IT procurement, project management, and coordinators to address department needs ● Supporting UTS risk management by assessing and mitigating financial risks ● Conducting financial planning and forecasting for UTS ● Balancing monthly ledgers for UTS Working with campus departments, including University Technology Services, analyze and evaluate multi-year and long-term cost projections related to total project costs for technology solutions. Unless otherwise required by an applicable collective bargaining agreement, all minimum, additional, and desired qualifications are preferred, but qualifications, degrees, and/or experience deemed comparable and/or equivalent by Oakland University in its sole and exclusive discretion may be considered. Job Open Date 07/02/2026 Job Close Date Open Until Filled Yes Position Specific Questions Required fields are indicated with an asterisk (*). Documents Needed to Apply Required Documents Cover Letter Resume Optional Documents 371 Wilson Boulevard, Rochester, MI 48309 248-370-2100     To ensure the security of your data, you will be logged out due to inactivity in 3 minutes at . Any data not saved will be lost. Click 'OK' to keep your session active."
