    "https://jobs.oakland.edu/postings/38887": {
      "title": "Course Design Assistant",
      "description": "Oakland University Employment Site | Course Design Assistant Skip to Main Content Employment Opportunities Toggle navigation Home Search Jobs Log In /Create Account Help Human Resources Benefits Campus Map Student Employment Course Design Assistant Bookmark this Requisition Print Preview | Apply for this Job Posting Details Posting Details Position Title Course Design Assistant Department 2163 - Center for Excellence in Teaching/Learning Position Number E12177 Requisition No. TC06499 Salary Range/Pay Rate $20/hour Benefits of Working at Oakland University No benefits are associated with this casual position. This is a general ongoing posting for an educational development coordinator with the Center for Excellence in Teaching and Learning, Employee Group/Grade Casual Job Category Casual Posted Casual/Temp Classification Work Schedule Casual (19hrs or less, No Benefits ) Shift/Days This is a general ongoing posting for a pedagogical partners coordinator with the Center for Excellence in Teaching and Learning. This is a part-time, casual position working 19 hours or less per week, most hours on campus during regular business hours. Pay Schedule Hour Number of Hrs./Wk. 15 Position Information Position Information Employee's Effective Start Date 09/07/2026 If this is a Temporary position, provide end date or enter N/A for any other position type. N/A Minimum Qualifications Bachelor’s degree. Foundational experience in developing self-paced online modules or courses. Familiarity with Learning Management Systems (such as Moodle) and interactive content creation tools (such as H5P). Ability to evaluate digital materials for accessibility and apply digital accessibility standards. Strong written communication skills with the demonstrated ability to synthesize information into structured documents, guides, and templates. Ability to collaborate professionally with faculty and subject matter experts to gather and refine information. Desired Qualifications Prior experience interning or working within a university teaching and learning center. Experience editing videos (using software such as Camtasia). Experience properly and transparently utilizing generative AI tools to brainstorm and draft professional resources. Position Purpose The Center for Excellence in Teaching and Learning ( CETL ) is seeking a motivated and innovative individual to assist our team in building engaging, self-paced online learning opportunities for educational development programs. The ideal candidate is a recent graduate with foundational experience in instructional design who will help develop online modules, create organizational templates, and support digital accessibility efforts. This position is essential in contributing to the center’s mission of fostering inclusive and effective teaching practices. Job Duties Develop self-paced online modules for university professors using Learning Management Systems (eSpace, Moodle). Design and integrate interactive online learning components utilizing H5P. Adapt live workshop presentations, recordings, and materials for an online audience. Collaborate with subject matter experts (SMEs) to guide academic content and teaching frameworks. Create course build processes, starter documents, and templates to assist future course development and future interns. Apply digital accessibility standards to course content, websites, documents, and videos using tools like Panorama. Job Open Date 08/28/2026 Job Close Date Open Until Filled No Position Specific Questions Required fields are indicated with an asterisk (*). Documents Needed to Apply Required Documents Curriculum Vitae (CV) Cover Letter Optional Documents 371 Wilson Boulevard, Rochester, MI 48309 248-370-2100     To ensure the security of your data, you will be logged out due to inactivity in 3 minutes at . Any data not saved will be lost. Click 'OK' to keep your session active."
