    "https://jobs.oakland.edu/postings/38608": {
      "title": "Position Information",
      "description": "Oakland University Employment Site | Admissions Application Reader Skip to Main Content Employment Opportunities Toggle navigation Home Search Jobs Log In /Create Account Help Human Resources Benefits Campus Map Student Employment Admissions Application Reader Bookmark this Requisition Print Preview | Apply for this Job Posting Details Posting Details Position Title Admissions Application Reader Department 0100 - School of Medicine Position Number E14245 Requisition No. TC06474 Salary Range/Pay Rate 20/hr Benefits of Working at Oakland University No benefits are associated with this position. Employee Group/Grade Casual Job Category Casual /Temporary Casual/Temp Classification Work Schedule Casual (19hrs or less, No Benefits ) Shift/Days Pay Schedule Hour Number of Hrs./Wk. 5-10 hours/week Position Information Position Information Employee's Effective Start Date 08/04/2026 If this is a Temporary position, provide end date or enter N/A for any other position type. N/A Minimum Qualifications A bachelor’s degree or equivalent combination of education and training is required. Strong time management skills Strong reading/writing skills Strong analytical and evaluation skills Desired Qualifications Some experience in higher education, secondary school teaching, admissions, or medical profession is preferred, but not required Position Purpose Admissions Application Readers will recommend which applicants should advance in the admissions process to the Oakland University William Beaumont School of Medicine. Readers will holistically review written application materials, carefully evaluate academic preparation, assess an applicant’s exposure to the medical profession, as well as their desire to serve others and their communities. Job Duties Readers are expected to carefully read and make holistic evaluations on two application files per hour. Application review is conducted online, allowing flexible working hours. Work will be expected to be completed outside of the admission office. However, readers must attend an on-campus training session, regularly scheduled meetings with other readers and the department supervisor. The Admissions Application Readers positions are seasonally used to review applications for approximately three to four months (July through December), but could extend beyond that period based on the volume of applications and departmental needs. Admissions Application Readers must exhibit excellent oral, written, and interpersonal skills in a diverse environment, as well as the ability to demonstrate a professional and confidential approach to the review process. Basic computer literacy and access to the internet is essential. Job Open Date 08/06/2026 Job Close Date Open Until Filled No Position Specific Questions Required fields are indicated with an asterisk (*). Documents Needed to Apply Required Documents Cover Letter Resume Optional Documents 371 Wilson Boulevard, Rochester, MI 48309 248-370-2100     To ensure the security of your data, you will be logged out due to inactivity in 3 minutes at . Any data not saved will be lost. Click 'OK' to keep your session active."
