    "https://jobs.oakland.edu/postings/35170": {
      "title": "Assistant Professor of Finance",
      "description": "Oakland University Employment Site | Assistant Professor of Finance Skip to Main Content Employment Opportunities Toggle navigation Home Search Jobs Log In /Create Account Help Human Resources Benefits Campus Map Student Employment Assistant Professor of Finance Bookmark this Requisition Print Preview | Apply for this Job Please see Special Instructions for more details. Qualified applicants should submit their applications electronically at https://jobs.oakland.edu/postings/ 34262. A complete application must include: (1) a letter of interest explaining how the candidate’s qualifications align with the requirements of the position; (2) a current curriculum vitae; (3) three letters of recommendation; (4) unofficial transcripts; (5) evidence of teaching effectiveness; and (6) a job market paper, along with any additional working papers or writing samples. Only complete application packages will be reviewed. The review process will begin on September 1, 2025, and will continue until the position is filled. Posting Details Position Information Job Title Assistant Professor of Finance Department 0460 - Accounting & Finance Requisition No. 0000781 Job Description Summary The School of Business Administration at Oakland University invites applications for a tenure-track position at the rank of Assistant Professor of Finance, beginning August 15, 2026. Qualified candidates must hold a Ph.D. in Finance or a closely related field from an accredited institution by the time of appointment. Applicants should demonstrate the ability to produce high-quality scholarly research and a commitment to excellence in teaching. Faculty members in the Finance area teach at both the undergraduate and graduate levels. The standard teaching load allows for meaningful research engagement, and the school offers competitive salaries along with excellent fringe benefits. Candidates with expertise across all areas of finance are encouraged to apply, although preference is likely to be given to those with demonstrated teaching expertise in financial analytics. Minimum Qualifications Applicants must hold a Ph.D. in Finance or a closely related field from an AACSB -accredited institution. Advanced ABD candidates will be considered, provided all requirements for the Ph.D. are completed by August 15, 2026. Special Instructions to Applicants Qualified applicants should submit their applications electronically at https://jobs.oakland.edu/postings/ 34262. A complete application must include: (1) a letter of interest explaining how the candidate’s qualifications align with the requirements of the position; (2) a current curriculum vitae; (3) three letters of recommendation; (4) unofficial transcripts; (5) evidence of teaching effectiveness; and (6) a job market paper, along with any additional working papers or writing samples. Only complete application packages will be reviewed. The review process will begin on September 1, 2025, and will continue until the position is filled. School/College & Department/Program Summary The School of Business Administration is AACSB -accredited. It has approximately 2,000 undergraduate and 500 graduate students. The school is committed to enhancing its instructional technology and global management efforts. For more information about the School of Business Administration see www.oakland.edu/business . More About Oakland University The University is located on 1,443 acres of scenic land in the cities of Rochester Hills and Auburn Hills in Oakland County, Michigan. The University offers 142 bachelor’s degree programs and 138 graduate degree and certificate programs. Academics include programs in the College of Arts and Sciences, School of Business Administration, School of Education and Human Services, School of Engineering and Computer Science, School of Health Sciences, School of Medicine and School of Nursing. As an anchor institution in southeastern Michigan that is dedicated to building ongoing, collaborative relationships, Oakland University embraces community and civic engagement to enhance the lives of its students and positively impact the broader community. Learn more about Oakland University’s Mission & Vision and Strategic Plan . Pay Basis Open Date 06/10/2025 Open Until Filled Yes Job Category Full-time Faculty EEO Statement Oakland University is an Affirmative Action/Equal Opportunity Employer and encourages applications from women and minorities. Posting Specific Questions Required fields are indicated with an asterisk (*). Applicant Documents Required Documents Curriculum Vitae (CV) Cover Letter Transcripts (unofficial) Writing Sample Teaching Evaluation Optional Documents Letter of Recommendation 1 Letter of Recommendation 2 Letter of Recommendation 3 Teaching Statement Research Statement Teaching Philosophy Other Document 371 Wilson Boulevard, Rochester, MI 48309 248-370-2100     To ensure the security of your data, you will be logged out due to inactivity in 3 minutes at . Any data not saved will be lost. Click 'OK' to keep your session active."
    },
    "https://jobs.oakland.edu/postings/38860": {
      "title": "Assistant Professor of Political Science",
      "description": "Oakland University Employment Site | Assistant Professor of Political Science - American Politics Skip to Main Content Employment Opportunities Toggle navigation Home Search Jobs Log In /Create Account Help Human Resources Benefits Campus Map Student Employment Assistant Professor of Political Science - American Politics Bookmark this Requisition Print Preview | Apply for this Job Please see Special Instructions for more details. Applicants should submit a cover letter, curriculum vitae, writing sample, unofficial graduate transcripts, evidence of teaching effectiveness, and contact information for at least three references through Oakland University’s online application system. Once all required application materials have been uploaded through the online system, references will be contacted through the online system to submit confidential letters of recommendation. Applicants may also submit teaching evaluations, a writing sample, and a research statement. Review of applications will begin on October 12, 2026, and will continue until the position is filled. Questions regarding the position should be directed to Dr. Terri L. Towner, American Politics Search Chair, at towner@oakland.edu. Posting Details Position Information Job Title Assistant Professor of Political Science - American Politics Department 1346 - Political Science Requisition No. 0000839 Job Description Summary The Department of Political Science at Oakland University invites applications for a full-time, tenure-track position in American Politics at the rank of Assistant Professor, beginning August 15, 2027. We seek a candidate broadly trained in American Politics with an active research agenda and a demonstrated commitment to excellence in undergraduate teaching. The area of specialization within American Politics is open. The successful candidate will be expected to teach an introductory course in American politics and upper-division courses in political behavior and/or political institutions (other than the judiciary), as well as courses in the candidate’s areas of expertise. The ability to contribute to the department’s research methods sequence is highly desirable. Oakland University operates on the semester system, and the standard teaching load is five courses per academic year. Minimum Qualifications Candidates with their Ph.D. in hand are preferred, but candidates who are ABD will also be considered, provided that they can demonstrate they are near completion of the dissertation. Candidates should demonstrate the potential for a productive scholarly research program, excellence in undergraduate teaching, and a commitment to advising and mentoring undergraduate research. Special Instructions to Applicants Applicants should submit a cover letter, curriculum vitae, writing sample, unofficial graduate transcripts, evidence of teaching effectiveness, and contact information for at least three references through Oakland University’s online application system. Once all required application materials have been uploaded through the online system, references will be contacted through the online system to submit confidential letters of recommendation. Applicants may also submit teaching evaluations, a writing sample, and a research statement. Review of applications will begin on October 12, 2026, and will continue until the position is filled. Questions regarding the position should be directed to Dr. Terri L. Towner, American Politics Search Chair, at towner@oakland.edu. School/College & Department/Program Summary The Department of Political Science, housed in the College of Arts and Sciences, offers undergraduate degree programs in Political Science (B.A.), International Relations (B.A.), and Public Administration and Public Policy (B.S.), as well as a NASPAA -accredited Master of Public Administration (M.P.A.) program. The Department also conducts applied research for public and nonprofit agencies through the Public Affairs Research Laboratory. More About Oakland University The University is located on 1,443 acres of scenic land in the cities of Rochester Hills and Auburn Hills in Oakland County, Michigan. The University offers 142 bachelor’s degree programs and 138 graduate degree and certificate programs. Academics include programs in the College of Arts and Sciences, School of Business Administration, School of Education and Human Services, School of Engineering and Computer Science, School of Health Sciences, School of Medicine and School of Nursing. As an anchor institution in southeastern Michigan that is dedicated to building ongoing, collaborative relationships, Oakland University embraces community and civic engagement to enhance the lives of its students and positively impact the broader community. Learn more about Oakland University’s Mission & Vision and Strategic Plan . Pay Basis Open Date 08/26/2026 Open Until Filled Yes Job Category Full-time Faculty EEO Statement Oakland University is an Equal Opportunity institution. Posting Specific Questions Required fields are indicated with an asterisk (*). Applicant Documents Required Documents Curriculum Vitae (CV) Cover Letter Transcripts (unofficial) Teaching Statement Writing Sample Optional Documents Teaching Evaluation Research Statement Writing Sample (2) 371 Wilson Boulevard, Rochester, MI 48309 248-370-2100     To ensure the security of your data, you will be logged out due to inactivity in 3 minutes at . Any data not saved will be lost. Click 'OK' to keep your session active."
    },
    "https://jobs.oakland.edu/postings/38346": {
      "title": "IT Support Specialist",
      "description": "Oakland University Employment Site | IT Support Specialist Skip to Main Content Employment Opportunities Toggle navigation Home Search Jobs Log In /Create Account Help Human Resources Benefits Campus Map Student Employment IT Support Specialist Bookmark this Requisition Print Preview | Apply for this Job Posting Details Posting Details Position Title IT Support Specialist Department 0570 - UTS Help Desk and Desktop Services Position Number X10570 Requisition No. TC06453 Salary Range/Pay Rate $25 per hour Benefits of Working at Oakland University There are no benefits associated with this position. Employee Group/Grade Temporary Job Category Casual /Temporary Casual/Temp Classification Work Schedule FT/Temp (40 hours, No Benefits) Shift/Days 7 am – 4 pm or 9 am – 6 pm, Monday – Friday Pay Schedule Hour Number of Hrs./Wk. 40/wk Position Information Position Information Employee's Effective Start Date 07/01/2026 If this is a Temporary position, provide end date or enter N/A for any other position type. 1/30/2027 Minimum Qualifications Two years experience working with computer hardware, Macintosh, Linux, Windowsoperating systems, applications, and peripherals. Knowledge of operating system security. The ability to quickly and accurately diagnose and resolve problems remotely based on customer information, including hardware and software issues. Diagnosing situations originating from LAN / Desktop out in the field and enterprise wide locations. Excellent organizational and analytical skills. Excellent oral and written communication skills. Ability to communicate effectively with others. Must possess a valid driver’s license acceptable to the University’s insurance carrier. Desired Qualifications Apple Certified and/or Microsoft certifications. Bachelor’s degree in Computer Science / Information Technology or closely related field. The ability to be flexible in a changing environment, with strong desire and ability to learn new applications and technologies quickly. Ability to handle difficult technical situations. Having an understanding of the university environment. Position Purpose This position supports the UTS Active Directory project for the campus. The OU Tech Center will be responsible for all Device Lifecycle, Asset Management and Endpoint Device Management – quoting, imaging, configurations, setups, asset tagging, planning, implementing, and supporting the university’s endpoint management environment during and after the migration to the new Active Directory. This position ensures that all campus-owned computers and devices are securely configured, centrally managed using tools such as Jamf and InTune, and integrated with enterprise identity services such as Microsoft Entra. The role develops and maintains device management standards, deploys support and automation tools, and implements least-privilege access controls to protect institutional data while enabling efficient support for faculty, staff, and students. Working collaboratively with infrastructure, security, and support teams, this position manages policies, configurations, and lifecycle processes for endpoints across campus. The role also supports the implementation of modern management practices, including device provisioning, patching, software deployment, and compliance monitoring. A key responsibility is ensuring that endpoint administration and support tools follow least-privilege principles and align with institutional security policies and regulatory requirements.Through effective governance, automation, and collaboration, the IT Support Specialists role will ensure a secure, scalable, and user-focused computing environment that supports the university’s academic, research, and administrative missions. Job Duties Analyze, develop, coordinate and implement desktop and notebook installations and desktop security practices. Provide campus-wide support to students, faculty, and staff for issues which include, but are not limited to, the areas of email, operating systems, network connectivity, applications, and classroom technology. Conduct technical troubleshooting, system changes and upgrades, faculty and staff technical training, and classroom technology support to the university community, in support of teaching and learning. Analyze departmental software and hardware needs, and recommend purchases based on analysis. Contribute to, and maintain, an internal knowledge base consisting of departmental processes and procedures. Construct and perform training on new, or changing processes and procedures. In addition, this position provides high level backup support to all distributed technology support ( DTS ) staff across the university community. Computer hardware installation, maintenance, inventory, software installation, licensing and upgrades along with serving as a technical adviser/consultant ensuring compliance with University policies and procedures as it relates to IT applications. Collaborate with vendors and other IT units of the University as needed. Deliver remote, telephone, in-person, in-person and on-line troubleshooting and diagnostic technical support services. Provide end user network support as necessary. Establishes and develops working relationships with new campus clients due to any organizational restructuring at the University. Liaison between Oakland University faculty, staff and students and the UTS department. Manage and coordinate IT technology service activities including: troubleshooting and initial resolution to help requests and incident management issues; elevating ticket requests, assigning tickets and monitoring until resolved. Provide software and hardware technical assistance and support for both Macintosh and Windows. Deliver remote, telephone, in-person and on-line troubleshooting and diagnostic technical support services. Install, configure, maintain and troubleshoot desktop hardware and peripherals. Perform basic network troubleshooting and hardware upgrades. Creation and publication of help desk scripts, materials and documentation. Working with growing campus client base on more complicated computing requests and support needs. Research and evaluation of new techniques, programs, processes, software, and hardware tools for internal Help Desk use and for a growing client base with increasingly complex technology needs. Responsible for setting standards and evaluating hardware for campus cost savings through partnership with campus teams and vendors. Job Open Date 07/13/2026 Job Close Date Open Until Filled Yes Position Specific Questions Required fields are indicated with an asterisk (*). Documents Needed to Apply Required Documents Cover Letter Resume Optional Documents 371 Wilson Boulevard, Rochester, MI 48309 248-370-2100     To ensure the security of your data, you will be logged out due to inactivity in 3 minutes at . Any data not saved will be lost. Click 'OK' to keep your session active."
    },
    "https://jobs.oakland.edu/postings/37228": {
      "title": "Position Information",
      "description": "Oakland University Employment Site | OUCARES Social Group Facilitator Skip to Main Content Employment Opportunities Toggle navigation Home Search Jobs Log In /Create Account Help Human Resources Benefits Campus Map Student Employment OUCARES Social Group Facilitator Bookmark this Requisition Print Preview | Apply for this Job Posting Details Posting Details Position Title OUCARES Social Group Facilitator Department 0917 - SEHS OUCARES Position Number E26182 Requisition No. TC06282 Salary Range/Pay Rate $30-$40 per hour Benefits of Working at Oakland University No benefits are associated with this position. Employee Group/Grade Casual Job Category Casual /Temporary Casual/Temp Classification Work Schedule Casual (19hrs or less, No Benefits ) Shift/Days Pay Schedule Hour Number of Hrs./Wk. 3 Position Information Position Information Employee's Effective Start Date 03/23/2026 If this is a Temporary position, provide end date or enter N/A for any other position type. N/A Minimum Qualifications Bachelor’s degree from university or college in social work, counseling, psychology, special education, or related field. Minimum of 2 years’ experience working with autistic individuals. Positive attitude towards autistic individuals. Ability to work independently and creatively with little direction from supervisor. Dependable, detailed oriented, organized and punctual. Must be a team player with strong communication skills and flexibility when needed. Desired Qualifications Master’s degree from a university or college in Social Work, Counseling, Psychology, Special Education or related field. Prior experience in facilitating groups for autistic individuals is preferred. Position Purpose Lead social program development and implementation with the goal of improving the quality of life of autistic participants and their families Job Duties Individual needed to lead social groups for autistic children, teens and/or adults. Includes supervision of all participants at the program, providing participant support when needed and communicating with the Program Coordinator on a consistent basis. Each class will be delivered on a weekly basis and could enroll up to 10 participants. Based on enrollment, multiple classes could meet weekly. Job Open Date 03/20/2026 Job Close Date Open Until Filled Yes Position Specific Questions Required fields are indicated with an asterisk (*). Documents Needed to Apply Required Documents Cover Letter Resume Optional Documents 371 Wilson Boulevard, Rochester, MI 48309 248-370-2100     To ensure the security of your data, you will be logged out due to inactivity in 3 minutes at . Any data not saved will be lost. Click 'OK' to keep your session active."
    },
    "https://jobs.oakland.edu/postings/38950": {
      "title": "Assistant Registrar for Data and Systems Support",
      "description": "Oakland University Employment Site | Assistant Registrar for Data and Systems Support Skip to Main Content Employment Opportunities Toggle navigation Home Search Jobs Log In /Create Account Help Human Resources Benefits Campus Map Student Employment Assistant Registrar for Data and Systems Support Bookmark this Requisition Print Preview | Apply for this Job Posting Details Posting Details Position Title Assistant Registrar for Data and Systems Support Department 2621 - Registrar Position Number 986401 Requisition No. S02788 Salary Range/Pay Rate $69,437 annually Benefits of Working at Oakland University Oakland University offers competitive salaries and an excellent benefit program including a comprehensive medical plan with low contribution amounts for our employees, dental and vision plans at no cost for our employees, generous paid time off plans, a generous University contribution to our 403(b) retirement plan, tuition assistance for our employees and dependents, free access to our Campus Recreation Center and workout facilities, and flexible work schedules and wellness programs. These are current benefit levels subject to future changes. Employee Group/Grade AP Band P Job Category Administrative-Professional Work Schedule FT/Reg (40 hours) Shift/Days This is a full-time position. First consideration will be given to those who apply by July 20, 2026. Pay Schedule Month Number of Hrs./Wk. 40 Position Information Position Information Minimum Qualifications Bachelor’s degree in a relevant field (e.g., Data Science, Information Systems, Business Analytics) or an equivalent combination of education and/or experience. A minimum of two (2) years of experience in data analysis and reporting. Strong analytical, problem solving and critical thinking skills with a strong attention to detail. Experience validating and reconciling data for accuracy. Working knowledge of SQL and tools to query, analyze and produce meaningful data outputs. Solid understanding of data modeling and data quality best practices. Strong communication skills, both written and verbal, with a demonstrated ability to adapt communication style to meet the developmental needs of colleagues and stakeholders. Demonstrated ability to foster strong working relationships, navigate differing perspectives professionally, and contribute to a collaborative and inclusive team culture. Able to manage multiple projects and meet deadlines. Proactive mindset with the flexibility to adjust to changing priorities and learn new skills. Working knowledge of desktop troubleshooting and user support. Desired Qualifications Proficient in SQL and experience with databases. Extensive experience with data model and best practices/standards. Experience creating dashboards and reports using tools like Tableau or Power BI. Experience with Ellucian Banner and/or DegreeWorks. Experience with Catalog, Curriculum and Scheduling systems, like Coursedog. Knowledge of higher education business processes. Experience building and maintaining ETL processes. All Qualifications Unless otherwise required by an applicable collective bargaining agreement, all minimum, additional and desired qualifications are preferred, but qualifications, degrees, and/or experience deemed comparable and/or equivalent by Oakland University in its sole and exclusive discretion may be considered. Position Details Position Purpose The Assistant Registrar for Data and Systems Support in the Office of the Registrar plays a key role in advancing the university’s commitment to student success. This position designs, develops, implements, and maintains digital processes, reports, and dashboards in accordance with established best practices, ensuring data integrity and reliability. The Assistant Registrar for Data and Systems Support develops and maintains comprehensive process documentation to support accuracy and consistency, and provides staff training as needed. In addition, the role supports enterprise applications and systems, including conducting testing and validation of system upgrades to ensure functionality and minimize disruption to operations. Job Open Date 07/07/2026 Job Close Date Position Specific Questions Required fields are indicated with an asterisk (*). * Are you currently a member of the Oakland University Administrative-Professional Group? Yes No No Response * Briefly describe the SQL queries or projects you have completed. Include the types of data you worked with, the tools used, the outputs you produced (e.g., reports, dashboards, analysis), and the impact of your work. (Open Ended Question) Documents Needed to Apply Required Documents Cover Letter Resume Optional Documents 371 Wilson Boulevard, Rochester, MI 48309 248-370-2100     To ensure the security of your data, you will be logged out due to inactivity in 3 minutes at . Any data not saved will be lost. Click 'OK' to keep your session active."
    },
